ESP32 AI Core Components
-Memory buffer
-Stores recent tokens or sentences (say last 128–256 chars).
-Text Generator Model
-Actual Logic script (Containing, the memory allocator for the 16kb buffer, the Parameter Referencer, Safety, ETC)
Lets Espie keep track of what you said and respond with context.
-Temperature sampler





Implemented as a circular buffer in SRAM.

Small generator

Instead of full transformer attention, use a lightweight feedforward + sampling loop.

Generates candidate tokens, stitches them into sentences.

Keeps runtime under 16–32 KB SRAM.

Rule set

Hard‑coded logic for safety, common sense, and basic tasks.

Example: if input matches “math” → route to math solver; if “sad” → route to supportive script.

Acts as a guardrail so Espie doesn’t drift into nonsense.

SRAM allocator

Manages 16 KB or 32 KB pools for buffers.

Ensures matmuls and sampling don’t fragment memory.

Could be a simple arena allocator: allocate sequentially, reset after each response.

Temperature sampler

Adds randomness to token selection.

Prevents repetitive “parrot” responses.

Implemented as softmax + random draw scaled by temperature.




onboot, allocate 16 to 32kb of ram
make it so it looks at 0x3A0000 for the dataset in 1.58 bitnet ternary or some bytecode format depending on specifically what the user say
look at the dataset (the dataset will be explained later of its format)
try to see what the user said,intention+context+ situation
then generate a script/sentence based on it.
then simply make it ready, and then output it


the only time it SHOULD ever uses ram is
looking/streaming stuff from 0x3A0000
making a small buffer to output text in
remembering what it said and basic context.



Dataset:
will contain a corpus or some small dataset (not finished, work on)
that will be trained over multiple times (thousands to millions of batches)
the dataset will be encoded within Ternary 1.58 Bit Binary for the smallest compact version or a Custom Bytecode because ESP32 flash limits are usually commonly 4 to 16 mb of flash 


Extras: this isnt a LLM, this is a SGM ( Script Generator Model)
and the modern LLMs are bloated (IN THE SENSE OF WHAT IT NEEDS TO RUN, E.G TERABYES OF RAM, GPU, ETC) and need
-Terabytes of ram
-GPU clusters
-CPU clusters
-water cooling
which raises the price of RAM, GPU  and makes the environment worser aswell

Espie runs on 16kb of ram and not 2TB of Ram   ( two terabytes of ram is 2,147,483,6482,147,483,648 KB,)
no real GPU at all, and a weird MCU Cpu thats commonly called the ESP32S3 (Commonly the XTENSA LX7)




